std::set erase uses std::_Rb_tree_rebalance_for_erase (a libstdc++
compiled-library helper); CBMC models it as the binary-search-tree erase plus
header maintenance, omitting the red-black rebalancing.  The iterator overload
is exercised here (erase-by-key additionally relies on equal_range).
